WEBVTT

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.750
What's going on, Morimoto?

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.150
It's really early in the morning.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:09.880
I'm sorry.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.360
I could have given you this in the classroom...

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.760
But I thought a quieter place would be better.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:17.720
Huh?

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:20.460
No way!

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.150
You serious? Isn't this place?

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.400
Sakakiba-kun.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.250
Morning...

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.650
Jun, be sure to lock up every night.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.210
And the table...

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.780
Clean it up.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:44.980
Okay...

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.280
But I didn...

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.450
Um, hey... Ryo-niichan...

00:00:59.130 --> 00:00:59.960
What?

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.360
No, it's nothing.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.270
Huh? Where's Shin-niichan?

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:13.450
I'm sorry, Morimoto!

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.150
What?

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:17.240
I appreciate your feelings for me, but...

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.650
Um... I...

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.030
But if you don't take it, I'll...

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:28.100
But... I... I like Megu...

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.220
Yo.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:31.830
Good morning.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.870
Hey, now...

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.670
Be more considerate, will ya!?

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.060
What's going on?

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.540
Can't you tell?

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.210
She's asking me out!

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.440
Uh-huh...

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:46.820
Um...

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.720
Kanzato-kun, just five minutes...

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.910
Oh, sorry. Am I a little early?

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.780
No, um...

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.630
What!? Were you trying to!?

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:57.590
Excuse me...

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.430
How do I get to the second-year classrooms?

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:06.360
Kanaru?

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.270
Mayuri... chan?

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.200
Sakakiba Takuro

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.490
kanjouni aragau nayo
Don't fight back your emotions

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.860
sono ashiwo tomenna
Don't ever stop

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.850
taoreru nowa mada hayaize
It's too soon to fall down

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:37.970
Breakin' through
Breakin' through

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:39.830
uchinukeyo
Pierce through

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.070
yamiwo hurihodoki
Free yourself from darkness

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:46.230
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:50.410
hurueru sora
Quaking sky

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.810
kazewa naniwo tsugeru
What is the wind telling me?

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:01.890
tadashii datoka soujanai toka
Right or wrong

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:04.990
kudaranai ronsouwa
Nonsensical arguments

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.630
kieya shinai kedo
Never go away

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:12.130
shinjita kotowo shinjinuku koto
Believe what you believe in

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:15.300
sono sakini bokurawa
At the end of it all

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.840
hikari mitsukeru darou
We will find the light

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.880
saa tokihanate ima
Now is the time to release it

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.810
kanjouni aragau nayo
Don't fight back your emotions

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.080
sono ashiwo tomenna
Don't ever stop

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.320
taoreru nowa mada hayaize
It's too soon to fall down

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.120
Breakin' through
Breakin' through

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.060
uchinukeyo
Pierce through

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.260
yamiwo hurihodoki
Free yourself from darkness

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:42.390
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:53.370
That camphor tree is known as
the spot for love confessions.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.580
I'd take it the wrong way if
I were in your shoes, too.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.950
See? I really thought...

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:03.320
At least you got to feel the rush
when Kanaru-chan asked you to talk.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.220
I got upset for a second when I thought
she was considering dating us both.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:13.090
Anyway, how did the test I failed
end up in Morimoto's desk?

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:19.660
And Shin, why did she wanna talk to you?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.470
I said...

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:24.370
I see...

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:27.980
That Mayuri-chan must be really cute.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:34.320
Yeah, she's up there. Even if you
assume all new students will look cuter.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:38.880
I even misplaced my test because
I couldn't stop staring at her.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.960
What's the matter with you?

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.150
Well... That Yamasaki girl...

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.130
I feel like I've met her before.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.460
Again?

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:55.900
This is the Home Economics
classroom. We're sewing a dress now.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.000
And that's the Science lab.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:00.940
Ooh, we've got a really cool anatomy model.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:06.610
It's got a pulsing heart with flowing
blood, an asymmetrical rib cage...

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.880
and the liver is exchangeable
with a cirrhosis-infected one.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.320
Right, Kanaru?

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:13.790
Huh?

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.690
She said that the human anatomy model is cool.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:21.260
Oh... yes, that's right! It's battery-powered.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.040
Hello, Jun-kun.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.950
This is Kanzato-kun's brother.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:39.810
Nice to meet you. I'm Yamasaki Mayuri.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.610
Hello...

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:46.110
Have we met before?

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.390
Sorry. I may just be mistaken.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.330
Well, bye.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.220
See ya.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.770
Oh, this is just great.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:09.010
I can't say who's better than who.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:12.810
I just wanna tackle both of them!

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.320
Hey, respond or something.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.810
I sound like a perverted old man.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.050
Yeah...

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.190
I really think I've...

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:25.950
What's wrong?

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:27.530
Hey.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.240
Was this tree like this before?

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:47.140
I don't know... If you say it
was, then I guess it was...

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:48.120
Oh!

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:48.450
Takuro
Oh!

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.250
Takuro
There it is.

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:54.390
Who the hell buried it so
everyone can see the score?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.460
That's crazy. How did they manage that?

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:58.980
Don't sound so impressed.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.330
We should meet up with the others.

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:06.130
Let's go.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.430
W-wait...

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:16.470
I have to go back to the dorms first,
and then go to my club meeting.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.550
You should come visit sometime.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:21.810
The dorm manager's pet dog is really cute.

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:24.020
It's super old, though.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:25.610
See you tomorrow.

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:26.720
Bye.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:27.650
Bye-bye.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:34.320
...Um, do you wanna come over to my place?

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.260
Someday, maybe.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.170
Mayuri-chan!

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.280
I'm fine.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:58.940
Once I'm all settled...

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.590
I'll come over.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:13.120
Morning.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.460
Hey, wait.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:19.970
Are you all right?

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.740
Owww... Dammit.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:24.510
What the-?

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.870
The school is... weird.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:27.840
Weird?

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:38.790
Huh? There's something in here.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:44.470
Kayano

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.030
Kayano
A P.E. uniform...

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:49.000
Kayano?

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.010
No, this is some kind of mistake.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.150
I see...

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.620
Of course rumors would start.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:03.580
Yeah, it's all over the place.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.050
Anything happening over by your classes?

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:07.450
Not at the moment.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:10.730
So what do you think about it?

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:14.680
Maybe a pixie did it while we were sleeping.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.860
I was asking a serious question.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.230
What else could do such a thing?

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:23.670
You went to see it, too?

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:26.100
Yeah. It sounded interesting.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:29.400
But that's what everyone is saying anyway.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:32.640
Like, aliens or... ghosts.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:37.040
Did you know? Our school
is built on an old cemetery.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:42.290
Oh right, you're not good with ghosts, huh?

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.490
Whatever...

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:51.870
Isn't the thought of a wicked,
tormenting ghost scary, though?

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:54.100
It's not like they cause explosions.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:57.740
There are wandering ghosts, possessing ghosts...

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.330
You seem to know a lot.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:03.580
But you're fine with Personas. That's weird.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.880
This is surreal.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.590
Quite surreal.

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:57.530
Look, isn't that the girl?

00:10:57.530 --> 00:10:58.860
I mean, she's...

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:08.210
The bell is gonna ring. Hurry back to your classes!

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:11.850
Persona?

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:15.380
It came up when I was talking with Jun last night.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.480
But what's being done seems so pointless.

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:25.990
Yeah, but it's more realistic for us to think
that way, instead of aliens and ghosts.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:27.750
True...

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:31.260
It sure doesn't seem like a human's actions.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:32.930
What?

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:34.140
It's him!

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:36.100
That flat-haired guy!

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:40.230
That flatty looked the type to do stuff like this.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:44.670
I don't really agree.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.950
Why don't we come investigate at night?

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:53.120
...No, nevermind.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.450
That's it.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.720
Let's see it happen for ourselves!

00:11:56.720 --> 00:12:00.130
If it's a ghost, then we'll take funny
pictures with it and go home!

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:03.730
Don't make it sound like it's some fun adventure.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:06.170
Something really wrong is happening, you know?

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:08.570
What're you gonna do if a ghost really appears?

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:12.230
Don't worry. I'll protect you!

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:16.540
There it is...

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:20.570
Hmm... whatever.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:40.100
A school at night is really like... a school at night.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.090
Yeah...

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:43.800
Don't back out now.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:44.510
What did you say!?

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:44.640
Um...
What did you say!?

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:45.040
Um...

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:49.210
Good evening.

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:51.180
Sorry I'm late...

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:55.020
What is it?

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.380
Are you trying to scare us?

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:01.610
Jun-kun?

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:08.730
I spoke with security and had
them disarm the security system.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:11.830
Hey, Takuro, you're walking too fast!

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:13.970
Are you listening!?

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:16.570
You can grab onto me if you're scared.

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:17.560
Idiot...

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:24.080
Hey, have you heard the rumor?

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:25.310
Rumor?

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:30.480
How all these things started happening
when Yamasaki-san came to the school.

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:31.990
Really?

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:36.720
I think Kanaru suggested this out of concern.

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:39.590
What was that!?

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:41.250
Over there! I saw something!

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:49.500
I swear there was someone...

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.910
Don't say stuff like that!

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:53.600
Y-you're scaring me!

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:58.280
Hey, Takuro!

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:00.820
Seriously, I can't take ghosts!

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:03.750
I thought you were gonna take pictures with them!

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:05.450
Not today! Today's a bad day!

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:08.120
You're not making any sense!

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.520
They sound like they're having fun.

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.290
Yeah? Is that right?

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:23.830
Oh yeah...

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.510
What did you need the other day?

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.440
That morning...

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:33.750
I had a favor to ask... but it's okay now.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.650
It wasn't about Shadow Extraction, was it?

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:36.950
What? No...

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:38.920
I-It wasn't!

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:42.590
How long have you two known each other?

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:43.250
Huh?

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:47.030
Yamasaki-san... She's kind of mysterious.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:51.960
We were raised at the same orphanage.

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:55.630
It's coming.

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:02.740
Do you hear that?

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:16.950
What the-?

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:23.590
Run!

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.570
Takuro and Megumi are coming to meet with us.

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:41.740
Are you okay?

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.080
Yeah...

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.570
I-I'm sorry...

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.630
It's fine...

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:28.290
Mayuri-chan!

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:58.090
Yamasaki! Hey, are you okay!?

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:01.530
Shouldn't we get the ambulance?

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:03.260
Y-you're right.

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:10.600
It's not going through.

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:12.740
What is it? Low battery?

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:14.000
Can't be...

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:16.740
We were just using it earlier...

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.410
Whoa, hey, Shin...

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:26.950
Where's Jun?

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:27.580
Huh?

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.350
No way, did we lose him?

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:36.000
I'll stay here, so please go look for him.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.030
But...

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.560
We'll be fine.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:40.630
Okay.

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:42.870
I'll try calling from outside.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:43.840
Okay.

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:45.540
Takuro, let's go.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:46.400
S-sure.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.010
A protective charm.

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:06.790
Mayuri-chan...

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.520
Are you looking for someone?

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.500
You must be lonely.

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:21.170
I'm sorry... This is all I can do...

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:51.160
Mayuri-chan! I'm so glad...

00:18:58.180 --> 00:18:59.040
Huh?

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:02.680
Jun-kun!
Jun!

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:05.590
Where were you?

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:07.180
I just needed to...

00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:09.850
It's over now, though.

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:14.700
What? Is it working now?

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:15.590
Hello?

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:17.800
Really!?

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.030
Yamasaki-san is awake!

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.310
Nothing's wrong today.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:30.040
I never would have imagined
the camphor tree was haunted...

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:33.910
But I'm more surprised Jun
had that kind of sixth sense.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:35.540
Haunting ghosts...

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:37.680
What is it, Kanzato-kun?

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:40.910
Personas are pretty much the same thing as ghosts.

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:43.250
Yeah? Is that right?

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:46.560
You two get way too scared!

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:51.460
I had this in my hand until I got back home.

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:53.130
Thank you.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.130
Good Health

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:00.770
Oh, this is Kanzato-kun's...

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:02.300
Oh...

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.040
See you later.

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.850
Are you better now?

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:09.650
Yes... but I don't remember much about last night.

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:28.060
I hope you'll find the person you're looking for.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.640
Make sure you hold onto her.

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:35.240
She can be dangerous.

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:41.480
Sure. Sunday, right? Got it.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:46.240
Okay. I'm looking forward to
seeing the manager's dog.

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:48.880
See ya. Bye-bye.

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.920
That thing is scaring me.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:55.860
Can you pull it back in?

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:03.000
Has your childhood friend changed at all, Saki?

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:05.240
Nope. There should be no problems.

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.740
That's good to hear.

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:08.500
Take this.

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:13.150
Don't you think you're taking too much of it?

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:15.340
You look better than I expected, though.

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:17.650
They treated me like I was a ghost.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:22.980
Are you gonna come back?

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:26.130
Or are you gonna keep playing school?

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:27.620
I may have found him.

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:29.250
Are you talking about Toma?

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:32.530
No...

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:37.840
I think I'll keep playing school a little while longer.

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:53.290
omotai kusariwo
The heavy chain

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:58.960
ima hazushite agemashou
I will take it off for you

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:04.130
jiyuuni naretara
Once you're free

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:10.900
kokowo habataite yukeruwa
You'll be able to fly away

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:17.850
atashiga samatage
I stood in your way

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:26.550
ubatte kita madaminu sekai e
and took that world you haven't seen

00:22:26.550 --> 00:22:31.020
tamerau nonara
If you're going to hesitate

00:22:31.020 --> 00:22:39.730
huriharatte ageru sono udewo
I will free that arm for you

00:22:39.730 --> 00:22:44.170
soshite tookue
Then to faraway

00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:50.340
dekirudake tookue
As far away as possible

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:53.650
aishiteruno
"I love you"

00:22:53.650 --> 00:22:57.220
ikanaideyo
"Don't leave me"

00:22:57.220 --> 00:23:04.280
koware chaukara
I will break

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:15.700
Admiration

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:18.230
An unexpected visit by the pale phase.

00:23:18.640 --> 00:23:22.800
An abiding look to cross a subtle heartbeat.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.510
A bright and gentle afternoon.

00:23:27.480 --> 00:23:29.010
Singing

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:31.780
Consciousnesses flickering deeply.

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:36.850
An invisible broken heart everyone has touched.

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:39.290
The truth that she knows.

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:41.860
The truth that only he knows.
